---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Check recorded exchanges (history or a run report) against an OpenAPI document without sending any request

Usage: rustman contract verify [OPTIONS] --spec <OPENAPI>

Options:
      --spec <OPENAPI>
          The OpenAPI document, a local file (URLs are refused: this command opens no network connection)

      --from <SOURCE>
          `history` (the default) or a run report written by `rustman run --report json=...`
          
          [default: history]

      --since <AGE>
          Only history entries at most this old, as in 30m, 2h or 7d

      --grep <TEXT>
          Only history entries with this text in the URL, the request body or the response body (case-insensitive)

      --limit <N>
          At most this many history entries, newest first

      --fail-on-undocumented
          Exit 1 when an exchange matches no documented operation

      --report <FORMAT[=PATH]>
          Also write the report as json, junit, markdown, html or sarif, to a file or stdout, as in markdown=out/conformance.md (repeatable)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment whose secret values are redacted from the output (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory, whose history is read (default: search from the current directory upwards; outside one, the ad-hoc history)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
